<Base title="Privacy policy | HourlyTechs" description="How HourlyTechs handles website usage information, analytics and customer inquiries.">
<section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p class="note">Last updated November 24, 2026</p></div></section>
<article class="wrap page">
<h2>Who we are</h2><p>HourlyTechs is a technology support business based in Flagstaff, Arizona. This policy covers hourlytechs.com and its website inquiry features as they become available.</p>
<h2>Information we collect</h2><p>Our hosting and security providers may process technical information such as IP addresses, browser details, requested pages and request timestamps to deliver and protect the website.</p><p>When our inquiry form is enabled, we expect to collect the information you voluntarily provide, such as your name, email address, optional telephone number, business name and a description of the help you need. Please do not include passwords, verification codes, payment card details, medical records or other sensitive information in an inquiry.</p>
<h2>Google Analytics and Search Console</h2><p>We plan to use Google Analytics to understand website traffic and improve the site. When enabled, analytics may use cookies or similar identifiers to measure visits, page interactions, referral sources, device characteristics and approximate location. Google may process information according to its own privacy policies.</p><p>We also plan to use Google Search Console to monitor search visibility and indexing. Search Console provides search performance reports from Google; it does not itself require an analytics tracking cookie on this website.</p><p>For further information, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>, <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a> and the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>. You can also manage cookies through your browser settings.</p>
<h2>How we use information</h2><ul><li>Operate, maintain and secure the website.</li><li>Respond to inquiries and identify suitable technical assistance.</li><li>Understand website performance and improve our content and services.</li><li>Maintain appropriate business records and comply with applicable legal obligations.</li></ul>
<h2>Sharing information</h2><p>Information may be processed by service providers supporting website hosting, security, analytics, form delivery and business communications. We may also disclose information when required by law or necessary to protect rights and safety. We do not intend to sell inquiry information or use it for unrelated third-party marketing.</p>
<h2>Retention and security</h2><p>Our approach is to retain information only as reasonably necessary for the purposes described above, including legitimate business and legal obligations. Technical and analytics records may be subject to provider retention settings. We aim to use reasonable safeguards, but no online transmission or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure.</p>
<h2>Your privacy choices</h2><p>You may choose not to submit an inquiry and may manage analytics cookies through your browser or available opt-out tools. Subject to applicable law, you may request access to, correction of or deletion of personal information you have provided. We will publish a direct privacy contact channel when the inquiry system is enabled.</p>
<h2>Children's privacy</h2><p>This website is intended for a general audience and is not directed to children under 13. We do not intend to knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.</p>
<h2>Future booking, payments and remote support</h2><p>Appointment booking, payments and remote support are not currently offered through this website. Before those features are introduced, we will update this policy or provide additional notices describing relevant information handling, service providers and access arrangements.</p>
<h2>Changes to this policy</h2><p>We will update this page as website features and information practices change. The date above identifies the latest revision.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/">Return home</a></div>
</article></Base>